  "$comment": [
    "Tamil and Indian-English names attached to EXISTING USDA rows.",
    "",
    "This file creates no foods. USDA already has mango, banana, brinjal and",
    "prawn -- what it does not have is the words a Tamil speaker types. Adding a",
    "duplicate 'Mangoes (Indian)' row would fork the nutrition data for no",
    "reason; attaching an alias points the existing row at a new name.",
    "",
    "That distinction is the whole layering: USDA supplies ingredients, curated",
    "files supply composite dishes, and aliases supply the vocabulary for both.",
    "",
    "One disambiguation trap worth knowing: USDA 'drumstick' overwhelmingly means",
    "CHICKEN drumstick. முருங்கைக்காய் is 'Drumstick pods'. The aliases below",
    "bind the Tamil words to the vegetable, so a Tamil speaker cannot silently",
    "log poultry."
  ],
